    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7764" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chasma</span></b> , ătis,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάσμα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an opening of the
			earth</i>, <i>a chasm</i>, <i>abyss</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 6, 9, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 4, 4,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">50, 15,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">18, 6,
			10</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of meteor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sunt chasmata, cum aliquod caeli spatium
					desedit et flammam velut dehiscens in abdito ostentat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 1, 14, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 26, 26, § 96</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. A. 9,
		20</span></i>.</div>
